# Administration

The **Admin** panel is only accessible to superusers. It is reached via the
**Admin** link in the sidebar, or automatically after login when no project is
assigned.

## Managing users

The user list shows every account on the system. Accounts that have been
disabled (removed while still holding annotation data) are shown with a
**Disabled** badge and dimmed.

### Creating a new user

Click **Add user**, enter the user's email address, and set an initial
passphrase. A passphrase is suggested automatically — use the clipboard button
to copy it, or the refresh button to generate a different one. Click
**Create user** to save. The passphrase must be shared with the new user
out-of-band; it is shown once and not stored.

### Granting project-manager access

Each user row has a **Make project manager** button. Project managers can
create new projects and add members to any project they manage. Click
**Remove project manager** to revoke this permission; the change takes effect
immediately without requiring the user to log in again.

### Removing a user

Click **Remove user** and confirm. The outcome depends on the account's history:

- **Deleted** — the account had no annotation data and was permanently removed.
- **Disabled** — the account had associated annotations and has been deactivated
  instead, preserving the data. Disabled users cannot log in.
